       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose of 2,550 mg/day. The usual maximum single dose is 1,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nThis may be a transcription slip. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily.\n- **1000 mg twice daily.** This totals 2,000 mg/day.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
